WEBVTT

00:00:12.804 --> 00:00:15.015
That was the worst delivery ever.

00:00:15.098 --> 00:00:17.851
Yeah. I'm never going
to another planet called Cannibalon.

00:00:17.935 --> 00:00:19.603
Me, neither.

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:20.979
Food was good, though.

00:00:21.813 --> 00:00:23.565
Great news, everyone.

00:00:23.649 --> 00:00:25.234
Shove it. We quit!

00:00:25.317 --> 00:00:27.903
In that case, I'll have to hire a new crew

00:00:27.986 --> 00:00:29.905
to go on our company vacation.

00:00:29.988 --> 00:00:31.114
Vacation?

00:00:31.198 --> 00:00:32.199
- All right!
- Whoo!

00:00:32.282 --> 00:00:33.575
This is great.

00:00:33.659 --> 00:00:35.827
I haven't had time off
since I was 21 through 24.

00:00:35.911 --> 00:00:38.205
It's just my way of thanking you

00:00:38.288 --> 00:00:40.707
for not reporting my countless violations

00:00:40.791 --> 00:00:42.709
of safety and minimum wage laws.

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:44.628
Aw! You.

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:47.256
I've booked us all on the maiden voyage

00:00:47.339 --> 00:00:49.258
of the largest, most luxurious

00:00:49.341 --> 00:00:51.218
space cruise ship ever built.

00:00:51.301 --> 00:00:52.719
The Titanic.

00:00:54.596 --> 00:00:56.473
Looks nice.

00:01:35.679 --> 00:01:37.181
Hey, where's my suitcase?

00:01:37.347 --> 00:01:38.348
Oh!

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:40.475
As mayor of New New York,

00:01:40.559 --> 00:01:44.146
it's my pleasure to introduce
the honorary captain

00:01:44.229 --> 00:01:46.565
for the Titanic's maiden voyage.

00:01:46.848 --> 00:01:50.644
A man who single-handedly
defeated the retiree people

00:01:50.727 --> 00:01:52.813
of the Assisted-Living Nebula...

00:01:52.896 --> 00:01:55.023
Zapp Brannigan!

00:01:58.026 --> 00:01:59.111
Oh, God,

00:01:59.194 --> 00:02:01.196
not Zapp Brannigan.

00:02:01.279 --> 00:02:03.240
You know Zapp Brannigan?

00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:05.742
Let's just say we've crossed paths.

00:02:05.826 --> 00:02:08.245
Was that before or after
you slept with him?

00:02:08.328 --> 00:02:09.955
She's a beautiful ship, all right.

00:02:10.038 --> 00:02:11.915
Shapely, seductive.

00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:14.626
I'm going to fly her brains out.

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:19.881
And now, without further ado,

00:02:19.965 --> 00:02:22.843
I christen this ship Titanic.

00:02:24.302 --> 00:02:25.429
Mmm-hmm.

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:35.047
Well, well, well,

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:36.840
the Lady Leela.

00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:37.966
Take notes, Kif.

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:41.303
You're about to witness the subtle waltz
known as seduction.

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:44.969
So, trapped on a ship with me.

00:02:45.307 --> 00:02:49.353
What say you and I
knock some very sensual boots?

00:02:49.436 --> 00:02:52.064
It's tempting but, uh,

00:02:52.147 --> 00:02:54.024
I have a fiancé now.

00:02:54.232 --> 00:02:55.776
Uh... Um... Uh...

00:02:55.984 --> 00:02:57.194
Um... Uh...

00:02:57.444 --> 00:02:58.528
Him!

00:02:58.612 --> 00:03:01.198
Fry, darling, meet Zapp Brannigan.

00:03:01.907 --> 00:03:03.158
Huh?

00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:04.534
How do you do?

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:05.994
Hmm.

00:03:17.965 --> 00:03:20.133
Ah! Here's my stateroom.

00:03:23.679 --> 00:03:24.972
Rawrr!

00:03:34.147 --> 00:03:36.316
Where is it? Come on.

00:03:37.125 --> 00:03:38.168
Oh!

00:03:38.485 --> 00:03:39.945
Now, Hermes,

00:03:40.028 --> 00:03:41.655
you and your lovely wife LaBarbara

00:03:41.738 --> 00:03:43.198
have the suite through there.

00:03:43.282 --> 00:03:45.033
And Dr. Zoidberg,

00:03:45.117 --> 00:03:47.119
your marble tank is on the other side.

00:03:47.202 --> 00:03:49.162
Man, first class seems nice.

00:03:49.246 --> 00:03:53.250
It'll seem even nicer
once you've seen your room.

00:03:53.333 --> 00:03:55.252
Looks like we're on the fiesta deck.

00:04:16.023 --> 00:04:17.774
This is it.

00:04:20.569 --> 00:04:22.112
Well, at least we get a window.

00:04:25.096 --> 00:04:28.099
Well, I'm tired of this room
and everyone in it.

00:04:28.143 --> 00:04:31.063
If you'll excuse me,
I'm going to pop over to the casino

00:04:31.188 --> 00:04:33.148
for the next 135 hours.

00:04:33.232 --> 00:04:35.776
I think I'll go fill up on bisque
at the buffet.

00:04:35.859 --> 00:04:40.113
I guess that just leaves you
and your fake fiancé...

00:04:40.197 --> 00:04:42.950
All alone on a romantic cruise.

00:04:43.033 --> 00:04:44.743
Take it off or I'll break it off.

00:04:44.826 --> 00:04:45.953
Okay!

00:04:46.036 --> 00:04:47.621
Captain's inspection.

00:04:52.459 --> 00:04:53.919
Mm-hmm.

00:05:01.552 --> 00:05:02.803
I'm betting it all.

00:05:04.972 --> 00:05:07.933
Come on!
Baby needs a new pair of feet!

00:05:09.101 --> 00:05:10.143
Snake eyes.

00:05:10.227 --> 00:05:12.563
Wait, my cheating unit malfunctioned.

00:05:12.646 --> 00:05:14.439
You got to give me a do-over.

00:05:14.523 --> 00:05:16.900
Sorry, the house limit is three do-overs.

00:05:16.984 --> 00:05:18.569
Next shooter.

00:05:20.279 --> 00:05:23.574
Give me your biggest,
strongest, cheapest drink.

00:05:23.657 --> 00:05:24.825
You got it.

00:05:35.127 --> 00:05:37.421
Allow me to introduce myself.

00:05:37.504 --> 00:05:38.755
I'm Bender.

00:05:38.839 --> 00:05:40.090
Charmed.

00:05:40.174 --> 00:05:42.009
I'm the Countess de la Roca.

00:05:42.092 --> 00:05:43.927
I was surprised to see another robot

00:05:44.011 --> 00:05:45.220
staying in first class.

00:05:45.304 --> 00:05:47.306
Most of the robots I meet are laborers.

00:05:47.389 --> 00:05:51.351
I assure you, I barely know the meaning
of the word "labor."

00:05:51.560 --> 00:05:53.937
Oh, Mr. Bender.

00:05:54.021 --> 00:05:56.732
Please, call me Bender.

00:05:56.815 --> 00:05:57.983
Oh, well, goodness.

00:05:58.066 --> 00:05:59.401
I-I don't...

00:06:05.449 --> 00:06:07.868
Kif, I'm feeling the captain's itch.

00:06:07.951 --> 00:06:09.411
I'll get the powder, sir.

00:06:09.494 --> 00:06:10.996
No, the itch for adventure.

00:06:11.079 --> 00:06:12.539
Prepare to change course.

00:06:12.623 --> 00:06:14.541
Sir, this is a leisure cruise.

00:06:14.625 --> 00:06:17.002
Our path was set by the travel agency.

00:06:17.085 --> 00:06:18.253
That's for schoolgirls.

00:06:18.337 --> 00:06:20.172
Now here's a route with some chest hair.

00:06:20.255 --> 00:06:23.800
But that course leads directly
through a swarm of comets.

00:06:23.884 --> 00:06:27.137
Yes, comets.
The icebergs of the sky.

00:06:27.221 --> 00:06:29.765
By jackknifing from one to the next
at breakneck speed,

00:06:29.848 --> 00:06:32.184
we might just get some
kind of gravity boost...

00:06:32.267 --> 00:06:33.519
Or something.

00:06:34.811 --> 00:06:37.773
It's time to shove a jalapeño
up this ship's tailpipe.

00:06:37.856 --> 00:06:39.691
Divert power from the shields.

00:06:39.775 --> 00:06:41.735
Full speed ahead.

00:06:42.903 --> 00:06:43.904
Oh, yeah.

00:06:44.655 --> 00:06:46.281
Amy! Hello!

00:06:46.365 --> 00:06:47.783
Mom! Dad?

00:06:47.866 --> 00:06:49.284
What are you doing here?

00:06:49.368 --> 00:06:51.703
We were planning
on enjoying a relaxing vacation

00:06:51.787 --> 00:06:54.248
but since you're here,
we'll have to do some meddling.

00:06:54.331 --> 00:06:57.251
We met the nicest boy
in the cabin next to ours.

00:06:57.334 --> 00:06:58.794
He's not very ugly.

00:06:58.877 --> 00:07:00.254
You should marry him

00:07:00.337 --> 00:07:03.215
or at least use him to conceive
a grandchild for us.

00:07:03.298 --> 00:07:04.675
There he is at the buffet.

00:07:08.887 --> 00:07:11.306
Uh... He seems really nice, but...

00:07:11.390 --> 00:07:13.851
Well, I already have a boyfriend.

00:07:13.934 --> 00:07:15.227
Really? Where is he?

00:07:15.310 --> 00:07:18.647
And why isn't he here right now
fathering our grandchild?

00:07:18.981 --> 00:07:20.107
Er...

00:07:23.277 --> 00:07:27.823
Well, our accommodations aren't great,
but it sure is beautiful out here.

00:07:27.906 --> 00:07:29.741
Yeah. It's pretty romantic.

00:07:29.825 --> 00:07:30.868
I mean platonic.

00:07:30.951 --> 00:07:33.245
That sure is one platonic view.

00:07:33.328 --> 00:07:34.913
Fry, just be quiet.

00:07:34.997 --> 00:07:37.249
I'm beginning to think
this whole fake fiancé thing

00:07:37.332 --> 00:07:39.418
was a terrible, terrible...

00:07:39.501 --> 00:07:40.586
Hmm?

00:07:40.752 --> 00:07:41.795
Mmm!

00:07:41.879 --> 00:07:44.256
Leela, perhaps this is an awkward time,

00:07:44.339 --> 00:07:47.634
but if things don't work out
with this pip-squeak here,

00:07:47.718 --> 00:07:51.930
I just want you to know
I'll be there to score you on the rebound.

00:07:54.183 --> 00:07:55.434
Uh, look.

00:07:55.517 --> 00:07:59.146
Before you get any crazy ideas,
that was for Zapp.

00:07:59.229 --> 00:08:01.273
Well, you got anything else for him?

00:08:01.356 --> 00:08:04.943
All right.
Can we try not to complicate this?

00:08:05.027 --> 00:08:06.737
Mom, Dad,

00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:08.322
I'd like you to meet Fry,

00:08:08.405 --> 00:08:09.531
my boyfriend.

00:08:09.698 --> 00:08:10.699
Hmm?

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:12.367
Mmm!

00:08:24.004 --> 00:08:25.839
See you later, wuv-ums.

00:08:29.176 --> 00:08:30.928
It would've been nice if you'd told me

00:08:31.011 --> 00:08:32.262
you were going out with Amy.

00:08:32.346 --> 00:08:33.639
I'm not going out with Amy.

00:08:33.722 --> 00:08:35.182
It's just to fool her parents.

00:08:35.265 --> 00:08:36.808
Hey, you're not jealous, are you?

00:08:36.892 --> 00:08:38.310
What?

00:08:38.393 --> 00:08:40.729
No, no, of course not.

00:08:40.812 --> 00:08:43.148
Good. 'cause I consider
my fake relationship with you

00:08:43.273 --> 00:08:44.691
a lot more meaningful.

00:08:44.775 --> 00:08:47.861
Mind if I freshen up
a bit before we go out?

00:08:47.945 --> 00:08:51.031
I was just about to suggest
the same thing.

00:09:02.626 --> 00:09:03.961
Pay dirt.

00:09:07.756 --> 00:09:09.258
Lovely, isn't it?

00:09:09.341 --> 00:09:10.926
Yeah.

00:09:11.009 --> 00:09:13.637
But only 93% as lovely as you.

00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:15.222
Oh, Bender.

00:09:15.305 --> 00:09:16.932
Either that was a computing error

00:09:17.015 --> 00:09:19.518
or you're the most
romantic robot I've ever met.

00:09:22.304 --> 00:09:23.722
I don't get it, iZac.

00:09:23.806 --> 00:09:27.684
That bracelet had a diamond
the size of a raccoon's brain.

00:09:27.768 --> 00:09:29.436
Why couldn't I steal it?

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:31.021
It's obvious, Mr. B.

00:09:31.104 --> 00:09:32.231
You're in love.

00:09:32.314 --> 00:09:34.233
Oh, it's true.

00:09:34.316 --> 00:09:36.360
But we're star-crossed robots.

00:09:36.443 --> 00:09:37.778
She, a countess,

00:09:37.861 --> 00:09:40.197
built with a silver spoon in her mouth.

00:09:40.280 --> 00:09:43.909
And me, just a regular honest Joe.

00:09:43.992 --> 00:09:45.702
Hey, you going to pay for those?

00:09:45.786 --> 00:09:46.829
Hell, no.

00:09:46.912 --> 00:09:48.372
Security to bar area.

00:09:48.455 --> 00:09:49.998
Security to bar area.

00:09:51.458 --> 00:09:52.918
Fellas, please,

00:09:53.001 --> 00:09:54.336
I'm in love.

00:09:54.419 --> 00:09:55.963
Rough him up.

00:10:01.135 --> 00:10:02.427
What are you doing?

00:10:02.511 --> 00:10:05.222
This penniless chump
was stealing drinks, ma'am.

00:10:05.305 --> 00:10:06.807
I see.

00:10:06.890 --> 00:10:08.308
Here you are, sir.

00:10:08.392 --> 00:10:09.643
Keep the change.

00:10:09.726 --> 00:10:10.936
You got it.

00:10:22.614 --> 00:10:23.699
Go, Professor!

00:10:23.782 --> 00:10:24.992
Lean back more!

00:10:27.411 --> 00:10:28.495
Ow!

00:10:28.833 --> 00:10:29.959
Come on, Hermes.

00:10:30.021 --> 00:10:31.832
You could out-limbo all of these people.

00:10:31.915 --> 00:10:33.792
Don't be a dog hot, woman.

00:10:33.876 --> 00:10:35.085
You know I can't.

00:10:35.169 --> 00:10:36.962
Not after what happened.

00:10:38.464 --> 00:10:42.885
Now limboing for
the Earth team... Hermes Conrad.

00:10:42.968 --> 00:10:44.595
You're my hero, Hermes!

00:10:44.678 --> 00:10:46.722
I'm going to be just like you.

00:10:46.905 --> 00:10:49.074
No, boy, stop!

00:10:49.157 --> 00:10:50.284
It's too low!

00:10:50.367 --> 00:10:52.327
Your backbone can't take it!

00:10:52.411 --> 00:10:53.994
I'm just like Hermes!

00:10:54.019 --> 00:10:55.270
I'm just like...

00:10:57.124 --> 00:10:59.042
No!

00:11:01.420 --> 00:11:02.504
There, there.

00:11:02.629 --> 00:11:04.590
Now you don't have to
limbo if you don't want.

00:11:04.715 --> 00:11:06.967
It doesn't make you any less of a man.

00:11:07.050 --> 00:11:09.136
Though it did get me some action.

00:11:09.219 --> 00:11:12.806
I like a man who's flexible.

00:11:12.890 --> 00:11:14.349
Your attention, please.

00:11:14.433 --> 00:11:16.059
As captain of this vessel,

00:11:16.143 --> 00:11:19.062
the terrible burden
of naming a limbo contest winner

00:11:19.146 --> 00:11:21.315
is mine and mine alone.

00:11:21.398 --> 00:11:23.567
Shouldn't you be steering
between the comets?

00:11:23.650 --> 00:11:25.110
And the winner is...

00:11:25.193 --> 00:11:26.570
Leela.

00:11:28.071 --> 00:11:29.656
But I didn't even limbo.

00:11:29.740 --> 00:11:30.824
No matter.

00:11:30.849 --> 00:11:34.561
I know from personal experience
how horizontal you can get.

00:11:34.745 --> 00:11:36.830
As your reward, you and that hair pile

00:11:36.914 --> 00:11:40.417
are invited to dine
at the captain's table this evening.

00:11:40.667 --> 00:11:41.710
Whoo!

00:11:42.586 --> 00:11:44.755
Well, now you know...

00:11:44.838 --> 00:11:46.173
I'm not actually rich.

00:11:46.256 --> 00:11:48.342
I'm a fraud,

00:11:48.425 --> 00:11:50.969
a poor, lazy, sexy fraud.

00:11:51.053 --> 00:11:54.598
This isn't even a real bow tie,
it's magnetic.

00:11:55.891 --> 00:11:58.310
Bender, I don't care
whether you have money.

00:11:58.393 --> 00:12:00.729
I love you for
your artificial intelligence

00:12:00.812 --> 00:12:02.397
and your sincerity simulator.

00:12:02.481 --> 00:12:03.565
You do?

00:12:03.649 --> 00:12:04.733
Really?

00:12:41.728 --> 00:12:43.397
I like your style, Fry.

00:12:43.480 --> 00:12:45.357
You remind me of a young me.

00:12:45.440 --> 00:12:46.984
Not much younger, mind you.

00:12:47.067 --> 00:12:49.111
Perhaps even a couple of years older.

00:12:49.194 --> 00:12:52.114
- Thank you, sir.
- But as a gentleman, I must warn you,

00:12:52.197 --> 00:12:54.491
if you so much as glance at another woman,

00:12:54.575 --> 00:12:57.035
I'll be all over Leela
like a fly on a pile

00:12:57.119 --> 00:12:59.663
of very seductive manure.

00:12:59.746 --> 00:13:00.872
Well, rest assured,

00:13:00.956 --> 00:13:02.252
Leela's the only girl for me.

00:13:02.277 --> 00:13:03.092
Hey, Fry.

00:13:03.561 --> 00:13:05.043
- Amy.
- Leela.

00:13:05.127 --> 00:13:06.461
The family Wong.

00:13:06.545 --> 00:13:08.589
Our party is complete.

00:13:08.672 --> 00:13:10.048
What are we going to do?

00:13:10.132 --> 00:13:12.426
Fry can't pretend
to be both our boyfriends.

00:13:12.509 --> 00:13:13.802
Sure, I can.

00:13:13.886 --> 00:13:16.179
I learned how to handle
delicate social situations

00:13:16.263 --> 00:13:18.432
from a little show called Three's Company.

00:13:19.892 --> 00:13:22.185
I'd like to impose a toast
on the happy couple.

00:13:22.269 --> 00:13:23.604
Down the hatch.

00:13:23.687 --> 00:13:24.688
Hear, hear.

00:13:24.771 --> 00:13:25.772
Now let's have a kiss.

00:13:25.856 --> 00:13:27.316
Yes, Fry,

00:13:27.399 --> 00:13:28.984
plant one on your woman.

00:13:29.067 --> 00:13:31.194
Um... Let me think.

00:13:31.695 --> 00:13:33.030
Come and knock on our door

00:13:34.865 --> 00:13:36.783
Mr. Roper...

00:13:36.867 --> 00:13:38.869
What's the holdup?
Kiss my daughter already!

00:13:38.952 --> 00:13:40.871
Wait. I'm confused. Now, tell me, Fry...

00:13:40.954 --> 00:13:43.665
Which one of these ladies
are you involved with?

00:13:43.749 --> 00:13:44.917
Uh...

00:13:46.919 --> 00:13:48.545
Captain, may I have a word with you?

00:13:48.629 --> 00:13:49.630
No.

00:13:49.713 --> 00:13:51.006
It's an emergency, sir.

00:13:51.089 --> 00:13:53.008
Come back when it's a catastrophe.

00:13:56.261 --> 00:13:57.554
Oh, very well.

00:13:58.680 --> 00:14:01.808
Well, with Zapp gone
and my parents still here,

00:14:01.892 --> 00:14:05.103
I suggest Fry give me
a nice convincing kiss.

00:14:05.812 --> 00:14:08.732
Ah! Now there's something
we can all enjoy.

00:14:11.902 --> 00:14:14.947
- Sir, remember your course correction?
- No.

00:14:15.030 --> 00:14:18.450
Well, it's proving somewhat more suicidal
than we'd initially hoped.

00:14:18.533 --> 00:14:19.701
Kif, old friend,

00:14:19.785 --> 00:14:21.203
I don't know which disgusts me more,

00:14:21.286 --> 00:14:22.746
your cowardice or your stupidity.

00:14:22.829 --> 00:14:24.164
We'll simply set a new course

00:14:24.248 --> 00:14:25.832
for that empty region over there,

00:14:25.916 --> 00:14:28.085
near that blackish, hole-ish thing.

00:14:35.008 --> 00:14:37.177
Hey, Leela, why'd you run off from dinner?

00:14:37.261 --> 00:14:38.637
I didn't run off.

00:14:38.720 --> 00:14:41.390
I had plenty of time to finish eating
and stroll away

00:14:41.473 --> 00:14:42.808
while you were kissing Amy.

00:14:42.891 --> 00:14:45.394
Oh, look,
I'm not actually interested in her

00:14:45.477 --> 00:14:47.271
if that's what's bothering you.

00:14:47.354 --> 00:14:48.814
Oh. Are you sure?

00:14:48.897 --> 00:14:50.440
I mean, she has two eyes.

00:14:50.524 --> 00:14:52.150
You have two eyes.

00:14:52.234 --> 00:14:54.278
I know... we seem like a perfect match

00:14:54.361 --> 00:14:56.613
but I just don't feel that way about her.

00:14:57.263 --> 00:14:58.806
Nice nebula.

00:14:58.937 --> 00:14:59.658
Yeah.

00:15:03.078 --> 00:15:05.414
Looks like everybody's got somebody...

00:15:06.039 --> 00:15:07.499
except me.

00:15:07.583 --> 00:15:09.543
And me.

00:15:15.674 --> 00:15:17.175
Ow!

00:15:17.634 --> 00:15:19.219
What was that?

00:15:20.095 --> 00:15:22.848
Oh, my God. We're heading
straight into a black hole.

00:15:24.391 --> 00:15:26.351
Talk about a mood killer.

00:15:30.939 --> 00:15:32.524
Don't blame yourself, Kif.

00:15:32.608 --> 00:15:34.318
We were doomed from the start.

00:15:34.401 --> 00:15:35.527
Nothing remains now

00:15:35.611 --> 00:15:38.113
but for the captain
to go down with the ship.

00:15:38.196 --> 00:15:40.240
Why, that's surprisingly noble
of you, sir.

00:15:40.324 --> 00:15:41.909
No. It's noble of you, Kif.

00:15:41.992 --> 00:15:45.120
As of now, you're in command.

00:15:45.203 --> 00:15:46.788
Congratulations, Captain.

00:15:54.171 --> 00:15:57.925
Okay, we just have to get
from here to the escape pods.

00:16:02.888 --> 00:16:05.224
I'm too young to die.

00:16:05.307 --> 00:16:07.142
Come on, before it's too late.

00:16:07.226 --> 00:16:08.560
You all go without me.

00:16:08.644 --> 00:16:10.896
I'm going to take one last look around.

00:16:10.979 --> 00:16:12.814
You know, for stuff to steal.

00:16:12.898 --> 00:16:14.983
You're going back for the countess,
aren't you?

00:16:15.108 --> 00:16:16.735
All right. I am.

00:16:16.818 --> 00:16:18.362
But I don't want the others to know.

00:16:18.445 --> 00:16:19.529
If I don't come back,

00:16:19.655 --> 00:16:22.115
just say I died robbing some old man.

00:16:22.199 --> 00:16:24.743
I'll tell him you went out
prying the wedding ring

00:16:24.826 --> 00:16:26.161
off his cold, dead finger.

00:16:26.245 --> 00:16:28.330
I love you, buddy.

00:16:32.334 --> 00:16:34.086
Countess!

00:16:34.169 --> 00:16:35.545
Countess!

00:16:35.629 --> 00:16:37.005
Bender!

00:16:39.841 --> 00:16:41.468
I fell through the deck!

00:16:41.552 --> 00:16:43.637
Are you hurt, my sweet?

00:16:43.720 --> 00:16:46.974
No. Luckily, a family broke my fall.

00:16:47.057 --> 00:16:48.225
Just hang on.

00:16:48.308 --> 00:16:50.394
I'll take care of that fire.

00:17:00.779 --> 00:17:03.824
Bender,
you risked your life to save me.

00:17:03.907 --> 00:17:05.534
And I'd do it again.

00:17:05.617 --> 00:17:07.661
And perhaps a third time.

00:17:07.786 --> 00:17:09.580
But that would be it.

00:17:12.165 --> 00:17:15.627
When we kiss, I feel like
I'm standing waist deep

00:17:15.711 --> 00:17:19.381
in a pool of cold rising water.

00:17:20.465 --> 00:17:22.426
No!

00:17:25.429 --> 00:17:26.471
Hurry.

00:17:26.555 --> 00:17:28.849
The escape pods should be just ahead.

00:17:30.225 --> 00:17:31.310
Faster.

00:17:40.319 --> 00:17:41.695
It won't move...

00:17:41.778 --> 00:17:43.947
And the door release is on the other side.

00:17:44.031 --> 00:17:44.963
Then we're dead meat.

00:17:44.988 --> 00:17:46.990
No one could squeeze under there.

00:17:47.015 --> 00:17:50.078
No one except a legendary limbo champion.

00:17:51.330 --> 00:17:52.831
Oh, Hermes.

00:17:54.166 --> 00:17:56.585
Ooh! It's been a while.

00:18:00.422 --> 00:18:04.426
This one is for that little kid
who's limboing up in heaven right now.

00:18:11.750 --> 00:18:14.962
That's my man. All right, baby, limbo.

00:18:15.087 --> 00:18:17.464
I still got the moves.

00:18:17.548 --> 00:18:20.134
Zoidberg, lower the door another inch.

00:18:20.217 --> 00:18:22.511
Just go on through and hit the release,
You hot dog.

00:18:22.594 --> 00:18:23.929
Yes, dear.

00:18:26.431 --> 00:18:28.517
- That's my man.
- Yeah, Hermes!

00:18:29.768 --> 00:18:32.646
Uh, can somebody help me up?

00:18:36.608 --> 00:18:37.901
Now what are we going to do?

00:18:38.026 --> 00:18:39.444
Wait a second.

00:18:39.586 --> 00:18:41.254
Aren't you a member of the yacht club?

00:18:41.572 --> 00:18:42.865
By God, you're right.

00:18:42.962 --> 00:18:44.575
I'm a class-three yacht.

00:19:01.591 --> 00:19:04.344
Thank God there are plenty of escape pods.

00:19:04.447 --> 00:19:07.325
We won't have to dress up
like women and children.

00:19:09.628 --> 00:19:10.879
We can't leave yet.

00:19:10.904 --> 00:19:12.186
We've got to wait for Bender.

00:19:12.269 --> 00:19:14.730
The high gravity
must be slowing down his looting.

00:19:14.855 --> 00:19:15.939
Amy.

00:19:16.023 --> 00:19:17.566
Mom, Dad,

00:19:17.649 --> 00:19:18.650
you're alive.

00:19:18.734 --> 00:19:19.860
Yeah, but so what?

00:19:19.943 --> 00:19:22.488
The important thing is
we found you a new man.

00:19:22.571 --> 00:19:23.947
A captain.

00:19:24.031 --> 00:19:25.199
Mom, I don't...

00:19:26.138 --> 00:19:26.700
Hi.

00:19:26.784 --> 00:19:28.035
Hello.

00:19:42.082 --> 00:19:45.126
I don't feel well.

00:19:45.210 --> 00:19:47.170
Look, it's our nebula.

00:19:47.254 --> 00:19:50.006
Whenever I see it,
I'll think back to that moment

00:19:50.109 --> 00:19:51.860
when we almost...

00:19:51.925 --> 00:19:53.301
Never mind.

00:19:53.385 --> 00:19:55.136
Everyone else is off the ship.

00:19:55.220 --> 00:19:56.838
Where in Babylon is Bender?

00:19:56.863 --> 00:19:57.906
I don't know,

00:19:58.216 --> 00:20:00.260
but we can't wait any longer.

00:20:03.465 --> 00:20:04.675
Goodbye, Bender.

00:20:08.839 --> 00:20:11.069
Wait for us!

00:20:15.575 --> 00:20:18.161
Something's wrong.
We're two metric tons overweight.

00:20:18.577 --> 00:20:19.995
Well, it's not me.

00:20:20.078 --> 00:20:21.121
Look!

00:20:27.709 --> 00:20:29.212
I'm slipping, Bender.

00:20:29.296 --> 00:20:31.089
The pull is too strong.

00:20:32.608 --> 00:20:34.401
I can't live without you.

00:20:34.426 --> 00:20:37.053
If you let go, I let go.

00:20:37.137 --> 00:20:39.723
No. You have too much to live for.

00:20:39.806 --> 00:20:41.308
It may hurt for a while

00:20:41.391 --> 00:20:43.852
but one day you'll share your love again.

00:20:43.935 --> 00:20:45.186
After all,

00:20:45.270 --> 00:20:46.605
it's shareware.

00:20:46.630 --> 00:20:48.315
Don't talk like that.

00:20:48.340 --> 00:20:52.319
Tragic romances always
have a happy ending.

00:20:52.402 --> 00:20:56.656
Farewell.

00:20:57.908 --> 00:20:59.367
No!

00:21:07.167 --> 00:21:08.710
She's gone.

00:21:08.812 --> 00:21:10.356
But she saved all our lives.

00:21:10.420 --> 00:21:12.839
Without her,
we're light enough to get away.

00:21:19.721 --> 00:21:21.056
Don't cry, Bender.

00:21:21.139 --> 00:21:23.183
Nobody really knows
what happens in a black hole.

00:21:23.266 --> 00:21:24.851
It's possible she's still alive

00:21:24.935 --> 00:21:26.561
in another dimension somewhere.

00:21:26.645 --> 00:21:27.938
Right, Professor.

00:21:28.021 --> 00:21:29.648
Yes, absolutely.

00:21:29.819 --> 00:21:31.404
Not a chance.

00:21:35.337 --> 00:21:39.091
At least I'll always have her bracelet.

00:21:39.920 --> 00:21:42.010
What do you think it's worth?

00:21:42.719 --> 00:21:44.263
It's fake, mon.